  "line": "Mount Zion is the hill in Jerusalem that David captured from the Jebusites and made his city, and later the name is used for God's people and the heavenly city.",
  "moments": [
    {
      "title": "David captures the fortress",
      "text": "The Jebusites said David could never get in, but David captured the fortress of Zion. He lived there and called it the City of David.",
      "passage": "2 Samuel 5:6-10"
    },
    {
      "title": "The ark is brought up",
      "text": "Solomon gathered Israel's leaders to bring the ark of the covenant up from Zion, the City of David. The priests set it in the temple, and the glory of the LORD filled the house.",
      "passage": "1 Kings 8:1-11"
    },
    {
      "title": "The Lamb on Mount Zion",
      "text": "John saw the Lamb standing on Mount Zion. With Him were 144,000 who had His name and His Father's name written on their foreheads.",
      "passage": "Revelation 14:1-5"
    }
  ],
